{
  "about": "Orthotic topic-search evaluation for `python -m knowledge.evaluate --orthotics` (added 2026-10-22). It runs the app's own orthotic searches (orthotics/topics.py, with the case words) for the fake cases below and checks, per topic, whether a passage from the pages listed is among the passages the AI would see (RAG_TOP_K for a topic, RETRIEVAL_TOP_K for a gap field). The pages were found by reading data/extracted/<doc>.txt on 2026-10-22: VA/DoD stroke p. 166 is recommendation 13 (FES or AFO for foot drop, 'Weak for'); NICE HTG178 pp. 4-7 its recommendations, indications, efficacy and safety; Choo 2021 pp. 1-2 and 9-10 its abstract, introduction and discussion of AFO effects; ICRC AFO pp. 5-26 its design choices, trim lines, materials and EVA lining, pp. 9, 19, 23, 27, 35 its fitting sections; Fatone 2020 pp. 1-21 the outcome instruments (pp. 7-21 its tables: 10MWT, gait speed, TUG; p. 14 the Modified Ashworth Scale in stroke); WHO PIR module 3 pp. 11-30 the stroke package (gait training, provision and training in the use of orthoses); VA/DoD stroke p. 119 FES with gait training, pp. 68, 161, 167 its spasticity recommendations; WHO P&O standards part 1 (English and Arabic) pp. 62-63 fabrication and fitting, user training, product delivery and follow-up, and evaluating the outcome (standards 54-58); WHO P&O implementation manual part 2 (English and Arabic) pp. 101-102 fitting and customization, user training (preparatory and functional training, gait training) and product delivery. Widened 2026-10-22 after reading what the search returned: Fatone pp. 7-21 and the WHO standards and implementation-manual pages answer these topics too. A DRAFT yardstick for tuning, not held out; the owner may revise it.",
